WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Fly and N0tail have been playing MOBAs together for almost a decade.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:12.040
They've played on the same teams for most of their lives. In the same games. In the same roles.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.860
They've grown together, won together, and even lost together.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:23.400
But they've done something few other players have. Together they've built one of the most stable orgs in

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.540
Dota history.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:31.000
With four Major wins to their name. And it all started because the two men who led OG found a

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.680
brotherhood through Dota. A connection they wanted to share with a team of their own.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.420
This is their story

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:51.900
Tal “Fly” Aizik and Johan “N0tail” Sundstein met through video games, when they were 14.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:58.520
Fly grew up in Israel and Canada, with fitness and exercise as a core part of his identity.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.100
His father trained him in martial arts,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.740
instilling in him with a sense of how important discipline is to any serious competitor.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.820
And that became a core part of his leadership style.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.640
In Denmark, N0tail grew up obsessed with video games.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.300
That obsession developed into a dream, school.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.800
and soon he decided to dedicate himself to them full-time while he was still in high school.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.740
Fly and N0tail’s paths first crossed online in Heroes of Newerth,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.060
one of several MOBAs that cropped up between Dota and Dota 2.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.440
The pair eventually signed with a Fnatic roster that is considered one of the best in that game’s history,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:44.420
with wins at DreamHack Winter 2010 and 2011, and DreamHack Summer 2011 and 2012.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.640
But as HoN began to wind down, Fnatic’s roster transitioned to Dota.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.120
The team didn’t pick up too many wins early on,

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.900
but were a consistent presence in the Top 8 of various tournaments,

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:02.260
and most notably picked up a win against No Tidehunter’s soon-to-be-legendary roster at Thor Open

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.400
2012.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:23.040
(Casting)

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.680
Despite coming short of placing first at a significant tournament,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.600
the team was invited to The International 2013 and played well in the group stage,

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:57.320
(Casting)

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.720
Although their early tournament performance was respectable.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:06.360
The bracket phase of the competition proved to be too great a hurdle for Fnatic to overcome.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:23.480
(Casting)

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.800
The next season didn’t treat Fnatic much better.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.980
The team performed well at qualifiers and minor events, but the bigger, better teams always won out at premiers.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.660
But through their formative years

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.960
with Fnatic Fly and N0tail's signature styles became apparent.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.480
N0tail was the team’s leader. He was brash, loud and animated.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.640
"I'm here with N0tail from Fnatic or as I've now been informed, Big Daddy?"

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.580
"Yep, that's right."

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.360
"Why?"

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.280
"Why not?"

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.660
Fly, on the other hand, became a student of the game.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.400
He was the man behind Fnatic’s drafts and served as a calming presence for the team.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.780
"Even inside if I think I was probably going to lose, I would still say I'm going to win.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.640
Because it helps your mentality."

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.580
Outside of Dota 2, they were the best of friends,

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:15.680
but that chemistry alone, was not enough to carry Fnatic to victory, against the game's best teams.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:38.440
(Casting)

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:44.720
Fnatic would make it back to TI in 2014, but this time,  they bombed out in the group stage.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:05:00.880
(Casting)

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.100
Fly and N0tail were the first to leave Fnatic following their abrupt TI4 exit.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:12.560
The duo joined up with legendary Natus Vincere players Puppey and KuroKy and Alliance’s S4 to form

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.640
Team Secret.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:18.520
According to N0tail, the organization was supposed to be something different.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:23.600
Most Dota teams would switch rosters just days after a tournament if they didn’t win.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:29.140
Secret was intended to be a place where the players would work things out instead, and at first,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.160
it looked like things were going according to plan.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:54.400
(Casting)

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.320
But behind the scenes, that wasn’t the case.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:02.640
Fly was removed from the support role and pushed to position 2. He wasn't leading the team,

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.200
And he wasn't drafting.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.480
He was out of his element, and unable to show what had made him so valuable to Fnatic.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:14.840
"I've seen this before in other games as well, actually in Dota 2 as well. Where you build a superteam

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:20.080
and inevitably, one of the players is highlighted as the weak link as it were, and

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.520
he's been highlighted as that already, but it doesn't mean he's a bad player."

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.920
By December, Secret kicked Fly.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:34.560
Fly ended up wandering for a bit, playing for MeePwned, an EU stack, and eventually Complexity Gaming in NA.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:40.760
N0tail didn’t stick around much longer. By January, he was off Secret as well, and went to Cloud9.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.080
It was the first time Fly and N0tail ever played on different teams.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:50.760
From January to August 2015, the brotherhood forged by Dota was broken up.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:55.000
Neither player made any significant waves leading up to TI5,

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.160
but the tournament brought them back together, only on opposite sides of the battlefield.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.840
Complexity stomped C9 2-0 in the group stage.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.760
But both teams would end up drowning in the deeper waters, of the lower bracket.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:15.280
after a season playing apart with little success between them, Fly and N0tail decided that something needed to

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:15.880
change.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:21.240
Major and TI victories had escaped the duos grasp time after time.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:27.200
They weren’t young, rising stars anymore. They were veterans that had supposedly hit their peak.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.080
And they weren't going to get signed as a package deal.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:33.560
But Fly and N0tail knew that they were better together.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.680
They were tired of teams kicking players right after TI.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.760
The knee-jerk decision always seemed to make sense in the moment, but it rarely panned out.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.080
So they put their heads together to build something new.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:50.520
An organization that believed in working through mistakes and focused on developing

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.080
a core set of players.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:55.800
They built the foundation of OG; Monkey Business.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:01.240
"We wanted people to feel comfortable to be able to share whatever they have to say. And just you know

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.520
have some fun together while still working towards the same goal."

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.440
"So it was two different things combined."

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:11.160
Fly brought MoonMeander with him from Complexity, and the team went on to recruit Crit-,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:15.280
a longtime Danish player who had yet to get a big break on a major team,

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:20.040
and then there was Miracle- a pubstar with the highest MMR in the world.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:25.040
With Fly and N0tail's philosophy of positivity and perseverance fueling them,

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.480
the new roster announced themselves to the Dota world.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:09:07.260
(Casting)

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.500
After qualifying for the Frankfurt Major,

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:16.280
Monkey Business rebranded as OG and entered their second ever LAN tournament with tons of promise.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:20.720
Pundits felt that OG were strong, but too green to lift the trophy.

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:26.760
"In terms of LAN experience, the players individually on OG has a lot, but as a team, they've yet to perform."

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:31.740
"They were at MLG as their first LAN together and they went out pretty early on."

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:38.380
At first, OG proved them right. The group stage was rough and two losses to Vega Squadron

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.480
forced them down to the lower bracket.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:52.640
(Casting)

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.320
For any other team, that would have been the end of the line.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:02.520
The road to victory was too long and riddled with a gauntlet of Dota 2’s most dangerous teams.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.720
But OG was built to work through adversity.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:11.520
Fly and N0tail’s veteran experience resulted in a team that was made to work together and win.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:12.440
And they did.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:42.560
(Casting)

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:46.160
Mineski came next and crumbled under OG’s might.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:11:09.800
(Casting)

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:17.920
Next was Virtus.pro, OG’s first challenge, but OG rallied after a first game loss and took the series 2-1.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:51.040
(Casting)

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:59.800
After casting aside CDEC Gaming, EHOME, and TI5 Champions Evil Geniuses, OG had finally made it to the

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.200
Grand Finals.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:07.700
"It's been an incredible story, and the first team ever to come from the very first round Bo1 games and reach a

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.360
Grand Final at a Valve sponsored event."

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:15.340
There they faced Team Secret, the team that kicked Fly and N0tail all those months ago.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:22.960
The team that led them to play apart, the team that OG was built to be better than.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:13:46.540
(Casting)

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:50.360
Secret would momentarily halt OG's momentum in game 3.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:57.620
(Casting)

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:01.540
But in game 4 the Green Machine would not be denied.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:07.500
(Casting)

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:35.040
(Casting)

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:42.180
With that victory, Fly and N0tail lifted their first Valve trophy. To cap off the most incredible lower bracket

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:45.340
run in Dota 2's storied history.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.300
"A huge run, the dream run."

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.000
"Achieving what no other team has done."

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:56.300
"And no other team will probably achieve for a very long time."

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:03.040
Secret would avenge themselves at the Shanghai Major a few months later, knocking OG into the lower bracket,

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.560
which, this time, OG could not recover from.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.560
But despite their lapse in form, OG stuck together and kept pushing,

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:15.240
all the way to the Manila Major which they would conquer from the upper bracket.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:23.960
(Casting)

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:28.400
Things were looking good for OG in 2016, but at TI,

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:33.360
the team that had looked so good all year bombed out after back-to-back losses

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:37.940
to MVP Phoenix and colossal underdogs TNC.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:40.840
(Casting)

00:15:40.840 --> 00:16:11.940
(Casting)

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:17.460
"OG, eliminated on day number two at TI6"

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:22.500
"OG's early TI exit was a tough pill to swallow for N0tail and Fly.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:28.640
"I feel like as a team and myself, I wasn't able to get in tune with everyone. I also felt I was talking way less."

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:33.840
"This tournament, it brings out something like that other tournaments don't either."

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:41.760
"Like forget strategy part, doesn't matter you know we could be at like way better than other team but they

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:43.920
have that fire and we don't, we're gonna lose."

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:53.600
This time, change was unavoidable. Crit, Miracle and Moonmeander left, and were replaced by JerAx, S4,

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.440
and Ana.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:58.320
But Fly and N0tail – the heart and soul of OG – were still there,

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.560
and they had no plans of giving up.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:06.020
With their new lineup, OG bounced back from the disappointment of TI at the Boston Major.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:11.500
Only dropping two games en route to capturing an impressive third Valve Major title.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:16.680
"You guys redid your entire team, and you did it again. You two are the only survivors,

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:21.740
And that's your third Major! How? How's this possible? How have you done it?"

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:26.760
"It's definitely thanks to these three. No way and of course coach Séb. But ehh...

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:32.820
I mean we just just play like some oldies. You know we just made some rusty dota and then we get carried."

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:41.920
In Spring of 2017, OG attended the Kiev Major making it all the way to the Grand Finals.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:47.040
"They've never lost a major final either, and they've had three out of three so far, they're in their fourth final

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.280
as an organization. I wonder whether that will stay on as well.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:56.380
Their opponent, Virtus.Pro, came into the series hot. They had only dropped two games the entire tournament

00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:01.120
and were being hailed for their incredible flexibility and ferocious team fighting.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:21.160
(Casting)

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.440
"VP right now look absolutely incredible."

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:28.760
As the only CIS team in the bracket stage, VP had the crowd at their backs.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:38.360
And now face to face with the defending champions. They looked poised to drag OG into a bloodbath.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.160
"Will they be the ones to stop OG?"

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.880
OG took game one.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:19:10.160
(Casting)

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.720
But VP answered back by taking  two games in a row.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:20:25.440
(Casting)

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:32.520
Following game three, morale was low. But after years in the trenches together, n0tail and Fly weren't too worried.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.440
"Think about it this way, this is what I'm doing. I'm going to have another thousand Dota games.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:41.160
I might as well enjoy them, each one of them. No reason to be sad about any of them."

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:44.800
"Be happy that we're here, and that we have this chance. It's not over, nothing's over."

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.720
"It's a reset."

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.440
"How many best of threes did we do this?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.060
"Yeah it's just two more games, think about it."

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:53.980
And that positive never-say-die attitude was rewarded in game four.

00:20:54.240 --> 00:22:00.120
(Casting)

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:04.360
VP stormed out of the gate taking a commanding lead in game five.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:47.120
(Casting)

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:54.040
But through sheer will and determination, OG clawed their way back from the brink of annihilation.

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:58.000
(Casting)

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:18.160
(Casting)

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:21.000
From there, OG couldn't be stopped.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:54.580
(Casting)

00:23:54.580 --> 00:24:00.480
Unfortunately that win at the Kiev Major is OG's last premier win.

00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:03.480
Although the team struggled yet again at TI7

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:05.220
And the roster may have changed.

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:08.480
Fly and N0tail's philosophy remains the same.

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:10.360
"Treat people the way you want to be treated."

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:16.940
"Work hard. Enjoy the challenges in life and accept the failures along the way like they're there

00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:18.480
and you can't run away from them."

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:23.220
"Always do your best. And remember to always get back up no matter where you are in life."

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:28.020
Over the course of eight years, Fly and n0tail have grown alongside one another.

00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:31.340
And through the solidarity and friendship they found in each other.

00:24:31.340 --> 00:24:37.240
They assembled one of Dota's most stable, successful, and beloved organizations.

00:24:37.240 --> 00:24:41.240
(OG chants)

00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:47.720
Whether or not they win TI during their careers remains to be seen. But one thing that can't be denied is the

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:52.860
determination they've shown along the way to confront every challenge together.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:58.820
"Can't stress on it more, honestly these two guys are not only just in the game incredible, but out of the game."

